OL,3,GNEWSAHow a cleaner was wrongfully
OL,4,Aimprisoned over asylum seeker leaks
OL,5,
OL,6,FNorfolk Police arrested the wrong man
OL,7,Fon suspicion of leaking the addresses
OL,8,Fof asylum seekers which they said had
OL,9,Fcontributed to the recent disorder in
OL,10,FThetford. James Jobson was taken into
OL,11,Fcustody and charged ` only for the case
OL,12,Fagainst him to be dropped. The Crown
OL,13,FProsecution Service (CPS) has now
OL,14,Fapologised for a mistake which delayed
OL,15,Fhis release from prison and left his
OL,16,Ffamily distraught.
OL,18,FThe 62-year-old works for Serco, a
OL,19,Fcompany which holds the contract for
OL,20,Fhousing asylum seekers in the east of
OL,21,FEngland. He is a cleaner and lives in
OL,22,FCostessey, on the edge of Norwich.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
